      "text": "I'd like to modify Chel's suggestion of 10K people per new province. \n\n* **Instead of a fixed 10k per province, a new province by default will have 0 people. ** 1m or 10k people cannot come from thin air. ||I would have suggested the addition of a random X<1500 aborigines/natives but that will make this too complex.||\n\n* During province creation, we can decide how much population will be transferred from old provinces to the new one. The more the better, naturally.\n\n* Combined with recent growth rework, this will curb province spammers as well as put additional emphasis into planning, effectively discouraging province-vomiters (the equivalent of PS builds in DnS)"
